From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-broker: a swapchain in any present mode is presented as FIFO

The broker WSI refused every swapchain whose present mode was not FIFO (broker_create, from PS5_Mesa's
ps5/broker/radv-gpu-broker-wsi.patch at f7ce91ac4c3), though its chain presents FIFO whatever it is asked. Its surface
reports FIFO alone, so the refusal keeps to the Vulkan specification, but every Windows driver offers IMMEDIATE and
FIFO, and a program that names IMMEDIATE or MAILBOX without reading the list got VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED and no
swapchain at all. Wine's own vulkan-1 test does that for an ordinary 200x200 window and then ended on the swapchain
it did not get (PS5_Proton, vulkan-trace-111334 on the Pro, 2026-10-27: "gpu-wsi rejected extent=201x160 count=2
format=44 mode=0", both builds). DXVK and VKD3D-Proton read the list, which is why games presented. Any mode is now
accepted and presented as FIFO, as the chain already did; the extent, image count and format checks stay. Applied
after the asynchronous present's patch, to the same file; PS5_Mesa and PS5_Vulkan are unchanged.
---
--- a/tools/build-gpu-broker-client.sh
+++ b/tools/build-gpu-broker-client.sh
@@ -74,6 +74,8 @@
     patch --batch -p1 -d "$out/source" < "$out/patches/present-times-wsi.patch"
     cp "$root/tooling/gpu-broker/async-present-wsi.patch" "$out/patches/"
     patch --batch -p1 -d "$out/source" < "$out/patches/async-present-wsi.patch"
+    cp "$root/tooling/gpu-broker/present-mode-wsi.patch" "$out/patches/"   # any present mode, presented as FIFO
+    patch --batch -p1 -d "$out/source" < "$out/patches/present-mode-wsi.patch"
     cp "$root/tooling/gpu-broker/pw_present_retry.h" "$out/source/src/vulkan/wsi/"   # PS5_Proton's, beside the WSI
     python3 - "$radv" "$out" <<'PYWSI'
 import json,shlex,subprocess,sys
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tooling/gpu-broker/present-mode-wsi.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
++++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
+@@ -512,8 +512,10 @@
+ static VkResult broker_create(VkIcdSurfaceBase *s,VkDevice device,struct wsi_device *w,
+    const VkSwapchainCreateInfoKHR *info,const VkAllocationCallbacks *a,struct wsi_swapchain **out)
+ {
++   /* Any present mode is presented as FIFO (c->base.present_mode): Windows drivers offer IMMEDIATE and MAILBOX, and a
++    * program that names one without checking the list got no swapchain at all (Wine's vulkan-1, vulkan.c:975). */
+    if(!info->imageExtent.width || info->imageExtent.width>1920 || !info->imageExtent.height || info->imageExtent.height>1080 ||
+-      info->minImageCount>VIDEOOUT_BUFFERS || info->presentMode!=VK_PRESENT_MODE_FIFO_KHR ||
++      info->minImageCount>VIDEOOUT_BUFFERS ||
+       (info->imageFormat!=VK_FORMAT_B8G8R8A8_UNORM && info->imageFormat!=VK_FORMAT_B8G8R8A8_SRGB)) {
+       fprintf(stderr,"gpu-wsi rejected extent=%ux%u count=%u format=%d mode=%d flags=%u usage=%u\n",
+               info->imageExtent.width,info->imageExtent.height,info->minImageCount,
